ophie C. C. SunAuthors Info & Affiliations\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1137/18M1214305\n\nGet Access\n\nBibTeX\n\nTools\n\n## Abstract\n\nBarely set-valued tableaux were introduced by Reiner, Tenner, and Yong in their study of the probability distribution of edges in the Young lattice of partitions. We prove a generalization of a conjecture of Reiner, Tenner, and Yong on the number of barely set-valued tableaux. To do this we apply results of Chan, Haddadan, Hopkins, and Moci on jaggedness of shapes.\n\n### Keywords\n\n  1. barely set-valued tableaux\n  2. reverse plane partitions\n  3. toggle-symmetric distribution\n\n### MSC codes\n\n  1. 05E10\n  2. 68R05\n\n## References\n\n1.\n\nA. Buch, A Littlewood-Richardson rule for the K-theory of Grassmannians, Acta Math., 189 (2002), pp. Combin. Theory Ser. A, 158 (2018), pp. 66--125.\n\nCrossref\n\nWeb of Science\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n6.\n\nR. P. Stanley, Enumerative Combinatorics, Cambridge Stud. Adv. Math. 2, Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 1999.\n\n\n## Information & Authors\n\n### Information\n\n#### Published In\n\nImage: cover image SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics\n\nSIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics\n\nVolume 33 • Issue 1 • January 2019\n\nPages: 189 - 196\n\nDOI: 10.1137/18M1214305\n\nISSN (online): 1095-7146\n\n#### Copyright\n\n© 2019, Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics.\n\n#### History\n\nSubmitted: 17 September 2018\n\nAccepted: 20 November 2018\n\nPublished online: 17 January 2019\n\n#### Keywords\n\n  1. barely set-valued tableaux\n  2. reverse plane partitions\n  3. toggle-symmetric distribution\n\n#### MSC codes\n\n  1. 05E10\n  2. 68R05\n\n### Authors\n\n#### Affiliations\n\nNeil J. Y. Fan\n\nView all articles by Neil J. Y. Fan\n\nPeter L. Guo\n\nView all articles by Peter L. Guo\n\nSophie C. C. Sun\n\nView all articles by Sophie C. C. Sun\n\n#### Funding Information\n\n973 Project\n\nNational Science Foundation of China\n\n#### Cited By\n\n  * On the q -enumeration of barely set-valued tableaux and plane partitions\n\nEuropean Journal of Combinatorics, Vol. 113 | 1 Oct 2023\n\n  * Minuscule Doppelgängers, The Coincidental down-Degree Expectations Property, and Rowmotion\n\nExperimental Mathematics, Vol. 31, No. 3 | 5 March 2020\n\n  * Hook Formulas for Skew Shapes IV. Increasing Tableaux and Factorial Grothendieck Polynomials\n\nJournal of Mathematical Sciences, Vol. 261, No. 5 | 11 April 2022--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Tenner_B in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ATenner_B+in%3Amath)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; The elementary symmetric partition function is a map on the set of partitions. ... @misc{2504.13108, author = {Owen John Levens and Joel Brewster Lewis and Bridget Eileen Tenner}, title = {{G}lobal patterns in signed permutations}, year = {2025}, eprint = {2504.13108}, note = {arXiv:2504.13108v2} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... We, moreover, demonstrate that if an algebra is eventually commutative of arbitrary characteristic, then it has a finite basis of its polynomial identities, thus confirming the Specht conjecture in this particular case.\n\n  * On partitions associated with elementary symmetric polynomials\n\nCristina Ballantine, Shaheen Nazir, Bridget Eileen Tenner, Karlee Westrem, Chenchen Zhao\n\nOct 02 2025 math.CO arXiv:2510.01100v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2510.01100, author = {Cristina Ballantine and Shaheen Nazir and Bridget Eileen Tenner and Karlee Westrem and Chenchen Zhao}, title = {{O}n partitions associated with elementary symmetric polynomials}, year = {2025}, eprint = {2510.01100}, note = {arXiv:2510.01100v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nThe elementary symmetric partition function is a map on the set of partitions. It sends a partition lambda to the partition whose parts are the summands in the evaluation of the elementary symmetric function on the parts of lambda. These elementary symmetric partition functions have been studied before, and are related to plethysm. In this note, we study properties of the elementary symmetric partition functions, particularly related to injectivity and the number of parts appearing in their image partitions.\n\n  * Global patterns in signed permutations\n\nOwen John Levens, Joel Brewster Lewis, Bridget Eileen Tenner\n\nApr 18 2025 math.CO arXiv:2504.13108v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2504.13108, author = {Owen John Levens and Joel Brewster Lewis and Bridget Eileen Tenner}, title = {{G}lobal patterns in signed permutations}, year = {2025}, eprint = {2504.13108}, note = {arXiv:2504.13108v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nGlobal permutation patterns have recently been shown to characterize important properties of a Coxeter group. Here we study global patterns in the context of signed permutations, with both characterizing and enumerative results. Surprisingly, many properties of signed permutations may be characterized by avoidance of the same set of patterns as the corresponding properties in the symmetric group. We also extend previous enumerative work of Egge, and our work has connections to the Garfinkle--Barbasch--Vogan correspondence, the Erdős--Szekeres theorem, and well-known integer sequences.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMathematics - Scholarship - DePaul University Research Portal (https://scholars.depaul.edu/en/organisations/mathematics/publications/)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; & Tenner, B. ... & Catoiu, S., 2024, In: American Mathematical Monthly. 131, 6, p. 479-490 12 p.\n\nFilonov, N., Levitin, M., Polterovich, I. & Sher, D. A., Jun 13 2024, In: Journal of Spectral Theory. 14, 2, p. 597-618 22 p.\n\nResearch output: Contribution to journal › Article › peer-review\n\nOpen Access\n\n  * ### One-element commutation classes\n\nTenner, B. E., 2024, In: Journal of Combinatorics. 15, 3, p. 401-